diag(min13): progress blocks 30-40 through the rest of arm_init, keep the early console alive after serial_init, pause 700 ms before them

min12h29 (observation corrected by the Director): everything drawn up to block 29 vanishes in a fraction of a second, except block 29, even with the CPU stopped: something asynchronous started by serial_init clears the framebuffer. So: pause 700 ms (busy-wait on the generic timer) after block 29, then draw blocks after each remaining step of arm_init (kprintf startup 30/31, PE_create_console 32, PE_init_printf 33, cpu_machine_idle_init 34, PE_init_platform(TRUE) 35, ml_map_cpu_pio 36, cpu_timebase_init 37, PE_init_cpu+fiq_context_init 38, dram DT parse 39, just before machine_startup 40). On A5XELTE the early console is no longer turned off after serial_init (it would hide these blocks and any panic). Drawing only.

